# upstream/93-call-graph-iterative-construction: the call graph finds the
# callables of nested regions from a worklist, so its native depth does not
# grow with the IR's nesting, and the inliner, which builds it, keeps a
# small stack. A function under operations nested 10,000 deep, the graph
# built on a thread whose stack is 256 KiB: the function has its node
# (call-graph.cpp). The nesting is built in memory: mlir-opt's parser
# recurses on the same depth through each operation's parse hook, so
# through mlir-opt the construction is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "call graph: the function under 10,000 nested operations has its node, on a 256 KiB stack" \
  "$here/call-graph.cpp" 10000
